<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pierre Montet</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1885–1966</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pierre Montet was a French Egyptologist. In the 1920s he excavated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byblos">Byblos</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebanon">Lebanon</a>, uncovering royal tombs of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-bronze-age">Middle Bronze Age</a>, and from 1929 he directed excavations at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanis">Tanis</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile-delta">Nile Delta</a>. There in 1939 and 1940 he found intact royal tombs of the Twenty-first and Twenty-second Dynasties, including that of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/psusennes-i">Psusennes I</a> with its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> coffin and gold mask, among the richest finds in Egyptian archaeology.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pierre-montet.jpg" alt="Pierre Montet" width="320" height="379" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pierre_Montet_-_Buste,_3-4_dr._-_Egyptologue_fran%C3%A7ais,_Membre_de_l%27Institut,_Membre_de_l%27Acad%C3%A9mie_des_Inscriptions_et_belles_lettres_-_btv1b10219724w_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
